From e328543e1bec0fada8ac003e22736aac28c25c3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:11:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Classify unmatched lane cards with a bounded
 subscription fallback

Why: chat-created cards without deterministic provenance fell through to other even when lane descriptions identify their project. Preserve explicit/rule/inherited precedence and the existing gating logic, and preflight semantic routing before ordinary and origin-ledger write transactions. Shadow and nested graph writes never issue model calls. Helper and managed subscription routes are separately bounded to five seconds, unknown/error answers fail back to the default.

Proof: tests-first old-head run failed all four misfiled-title assertions; final focused canonical run passed 1676 tests across seven files, lane consumers passed 277 tests across sixteen files, seven semantic/timeout/body/transaction mutants killed, and scripts/check passed all 21 checks. Read-only live-card replay retained separately on task t_eeeeee000000003b.
